  I don't think ESA0 is a LANCE. Another box I have around here claims to
have an ESA0 device and its DECnet circuit name is SVA-0, while I'm pretty
sure a DELQA is QNA-0.

  On the other hand, a 4000-700A I have here (which definitely has a SGEC)
says the VMS device name is EZA0 and the DECnet circuit name is ISA-0.

>>   A DELQA uses I/O address 774440, while a SGEC uses 777500, unless I'm mis-
