  In a 3300, you really want an S-box DELQA (which would be the DELQA-SA
variant) which has the panel attached. This is for FCC emission reasons,
a regulat DELQA will work Ok as long as you make sure it doesn't fall out
of the backplane (it has to go in the upper pair of connectors, not the
bottom ones, so there's nothing supporting it).

  I think you'd get better info from the NetBSD/VAX folks, though -
*surely* someone must have tried this on a 3300/3400 already?

