:>In article <e3tvssggc5mga5a216peid5nqsfm27257m@4ax.com>, Richard <dr_vmsREMV@techieREMV.com> writes:
:>:I was trying to do a T64 5.0 installation and was using a RRD42.  It
:>:refused to work.  I kept getting a CHECK_MEDIA error message booting
:>:the OS or Firmware Upgrade.  
:>
:>  The complete text of the console error message would be handy
:
:? T_ERR_SCSI - CHECK_MEDIA/DEVICE
:
:Tried bumping the SCSI_RESET value up.  Nothing.  This has happened on 3 (!)
:RRD42-DE (I think) drives on two different 3000 machines (M600/M700).

