In article <8qql3m$spi$1@uni00nw.unity.ncsu.edu>, NetBSD Bob <nbsdbob@weedcon1.cropsci.ncsu.edu> writes:
:...So, I will have to replace the KA640 with possibly
:a KA630 cpu and then find a scsi controller for it and an ethernet card.
:The TK50 card and existing ram cards should be usable.  So, what should
:I be looking for...

  You will want a KDA50 or RQDX3 or KFQSA disk controller.  (I'd tend
  to assume the RQDX3 will have the widest set of drivers available.)

  RA (KDA) or RD (RQDX3) disks, and mountings.  Your existing RF disks
  (commonly found with the KA640) could be connected to the KFQSA.

  Your existing MS650 memory will not work with KA630.

  You will need MS630 memory, and the PMI memory cable.  The MS630-CA is 
  the 8MB (and biggest) memory module, IIRC.  Maximum of two memory modules 
  are permitted, and the KA630 system physical addressing limit is 16 MB.)

  DELQA or DESQA Ethernet.  (Not the DEQNA controller.)

  No Q22 dual cards can be inserted in the lower half of each slot,
  as the entire backplane is wired Q22/CD.

:The ultimate goal is to try to get either 4.3BSD or NetBSD on it.  
:Ultrix is really not a long-term option.

  I am not particularly familiar with the NetBSD/BSD stuff, nor with
  which widgets these support.  I will mention the availability of the 
  OpenVMS Hobbyist program.

 --------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
