In article <G1J4AG.70y@spcuna.spc.edu>, Terry Kennedy <terry@gate.tmk.com> writes:
:Tim Llewellyn <tim.llewellyn@bbc.co.uk> writes:
:> ...Hmmm, there was an ECO for VMS 7.1 for the AS255 related to RRD4X
:> and disk on the same SCSI bus, which cured a similar or possibly 
:> the same problem....

  It was typically the RRD45, RZ26F and certain other SCSI widgets in
  combination with the OpenVMS drivers for the 810-based SCSI interface,
  Fast SCSI, and SCSI errors and SCSI resets.

  The ECO referenced was:
    ALPSCSI01_071

  One potential workaround was:
    >>> SET PKA0_FAST 0

  ALPSCSI01_071 is included in OpenVMS 7.1-1H1 and later.

  I would encourage the use OpenVMS Alpha V7.1-2, and not V7.1 or V7.1-1H*.

  The original note was (AFAIK) around a console-level error involving an
  attempt to bootstrap off the RRD42, and I suspect that means it is not 
  related to the problem(s) addressed by ALPSCSI01_071 -- I sometimes see 
  a problem with certain Alpha system consoles (most commonly, in my case,
  a DEC 3000 series box) and the RRD42 "settle time", and have found that 
  a bootstrap off CD-ROM using the console environment variable SCSI_RESET 
  setting of circa 6 works nicely, as I have found that the default setting 
  of this variable (2?) can lead to problems when the console will try to 
  access the RRD42 too quickly after a SCSI reset.


 --------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
   Hoff (Stephen) Hoffman   OpenVMS Engineering   hoffman#xdelta.zko.dec.com




