I think you mean the VT105, which was a simple graph-plotter, not using
REGIS, and the VT125 which _did_ use REGIS, and was an add-on board to the
VT100. You could buy a VT125 per se, or a DIY kit to convert a VT100. I can't
remember whether that board would also fit in the PDT or VT103
PDP-11-in-a-VT100, but suspect not (there wasn't much space left!).

Later graphics terminals were the VT230 (B&W), VT240 (colour), and VT340, all
speaking REGIS. There are no REGIS terminals in the  VT400 and VT500 series,
to the annoyance of many.

